1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,488
Only 900 yen left for the month.

2
00:00:06,538 --> 00:00:09,500
Tanino Hayate. I can't leave this one out.

3
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:10,020
Ryo-chan.

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,780
But Nanakorobi is hard to let go of, too.

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:12,460
Ryo-chan.

6
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:14,518
So as the anchor for a trifecta box,

7
00:00:14,568 --> 00:00:17,620
Tanabota is the safer choice,
but then again...

8
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,160
Ryo-chan.

9
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:21,360
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
what's the big idea, all of a sudden?

10
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:25,040
It's not all of a sudden.
I've been calling you over and over.

11
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:27,660
Okay, okay, I get it. So what do you want?

12
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:31,313
Don't give me that.
I've got a ton of things to do,

13
00:00:31,363 --> 00:00:33,240
so don't make me waste my
time with your nonsense.

14
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,480
She's a terrifying
woman to have as an enemy.

15
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,460
Hello, this is Ryotsu.

16
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:40,640
Not again.

17
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:43,420
You want me to sell land?
Where is this land supposed to be?

18
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,920
Are you making a fool of me?

19
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,180
You can't sell what you don't have, right?

20
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,520
And don't sell it to anyone else, please.

21
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:50,860
Mind your own business.

22
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,900
Is it the real estate agent again?

23
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:54,980
Didn't they call yesterday, too?

24
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,200
Every day since the start of this month.

25
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,680
Why do they keep coming to me?

26
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,240
Isn't it about your family home in Asakusa?

27
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,460
Don't you have any other ideas?

28
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,160
Yeah.

29
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,580
Wait, other land you say...

30
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:13,860
Right, work's done for today. See ya.

31
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,168
Did I have some?

32
00:01:17,218 --> 00:01:19,000
A lead.

33
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,380
Yeah.

34
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:27,080
When you watch TV, turn the lights
on and sit back from the screen, okay?

35
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:40,220
Anyone who's broke, come see me.

36
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:44,980
I've got none either, but don't worry.

37
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:52,000
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

38
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:58,640
It'll all work out somehow.

39
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:03,940
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

40
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,120
So just shut up and follow me!

41
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,100
1 billion yen

42
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,660
Hurry, Bramating!

43
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,360
We have to save Matsuzaka!

44
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:31,580
Old man

45
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,360
How am I supposed to live?

46
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,380
What are you doing?

47
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,400
Lazing around in broad daylight like that!

48
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,820
Do some work for once!

49
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,420
Shut up! What do you want?

50
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:43,560
Our grandpa who passed away last year

51
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,940
Tsukudajima's old man?

52
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:48,060
Yours is still doing fine, right?

53
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:49,400
His younger brother.

54
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,280
You mean Uncle Minokichi?

55
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:55,140
Didn't that old man own some land?

56
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:57,800
We used to own quite a lot of land,
you know.

57
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:01,640
This place was originally
Uncle Minokichi's house.

58
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:07,740
But that boozing, gambling wastrel sold off the land piece by piece,
so it should all be gone.

59
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:10,380
So some of that land must
have been left somewhere.

60
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:10,840
What?

61
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,419
And for some reason, the real estate agent

62
00:03:13,469 --> 00:03:16,260
thinks I'm the owner of that land.

63
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:20,300
If I play my cards right,
that land could sell for tens of millions.

64
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,620
What? Tens of millions?

65
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:26,160
Minokichi's belongings are here, right?

66
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:29,280
Yeah, after the funeral,
Yone cleaned them up, I think.

67
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:30,840
Mom!

68
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:31,800
No, wait.

69
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,960
Dad, that old man never
married his whole life, did he?

70
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:36,544
Yeah,

71
00:03:36,594 --> 00:03:39,980
if Mom or the relatives find out,
it'll turn into a big deal.

72
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:44,020
Dad and I will handle this together.

73
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:47,960
That way, we can split the money from
the land sale between the two of us.

74
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:52,420
You haven't changed your way of
thinking one bit since you were a kid.

75
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:53,820
You're against it?

76
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:54,740
No...

77
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,020
Alright!

78
00:03:57,940 --> 00:04:00,560
This is my elementary school report card.

79
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,440
Don't keep such worthless stuff.

80
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:06,380
Mom keeps everything old.

81
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:08,660
It's an album.

82
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:12,460
Dad was young once too

83
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:18,300
I was so popular with the ladies that Mom was jealous all the time,
it was a real pain.

84
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,600
You can say anything about the old days.

85
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:23,640
If you don't believe me, go ask Mom.

86
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,500
Just hurry up and find the land deed.

87
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:31,340
You two!

88
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:34,160
What have you been doing this whole time?

89
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,720
Looking for something?

90
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:41,840
Well, we're looking for those patches
that were popular back in the day.

91
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:42,420
Right?

92
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:44,622
Y-yeah, that's right. Right now,

93
00:04:44,672 --> 00:04:47,800
old patches are selling
for quite a lot of money.

94
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:50,112
Patches? Well, whatever, just

95
00:04:50,162 --> 00:04:52,800
put everything back
properly when you're done.

96
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,300
A-all right.

97
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:00,041
What's with the
"patches" nonsense? Hurry up, or

98
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:01,980
Mom's got good instincts, she'll catch on.

99
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,620
I know.

100
00:05:04,620 --> 00:05:05,200
Found it!

101
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:06,380
Really?

102
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:11,140
This is the box Uncle Minokichi treasured.

103
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:14,640
Yeah, no doubt about it.
The deed must be in here.

104
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,920
That's not the deed!

105
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:18,820
What is this?

106
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:21,600
It's a glossy photo of Haru Setsuko.

107
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,820
A glossy photo.

108
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,860
The rest are all movie actresses too

109
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,200
Figures, that old geezer Minokichi.

110
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:34,180
Underneath is a packed pile
of love letters from women.

111
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:37,100
Just like a playboy uncle with his hobbies,
as expected.

112
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:40,100
Broken pocket watches and old coins.

113
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,740
Why is there so much worthless junk?

114
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:43,840
Treasuring his junk.

115
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,180
Is this a report card?

116
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,320
They're all duds.

117
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,300
What a family of idiots.

118
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:53,080
Mind your own business!

119
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:56,100
Anyway,
let's search the back of it once more.

120
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,640
This is the title deed.

121
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:04,320
What?

122
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:04,920
No, well...

123
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,840
Dad, it's the land deed.

124
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:08,900
Really?

125
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:10,620
Where is the land?

126
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,640
W-where is it?

127
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:15,100
Kasumicho?

128
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:16,520
It's Azabu now.

129
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,220
What?

130
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:19,240
Truly prime real estate.

131
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:20,660
We hit the jackpot, Dad!

132
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:24,540
I see! Yay! Minoki Matsui-san is amazing.

133
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:26,640
Did you find the deed?

134
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:31,340
Thank you for coming all this way.

135
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:34,060
Sorry you had to call so many times.

136
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:37,060
It's old land,
so I'd completely forgotten about it.

137
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,800
I see, that's how it is.

138
00:06:39,800 --> 00:06:42,860
My father will bring all
the necessary documents later.

139
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:45,440
Let's hear the details first.

140
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:46,920
Understood.

141
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:50,000
This way, please.

142
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:52,160
There's a house here too?

143
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,620
Yes, this one in the middle
is the ten-tsubo plot.

144
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:58,180
A house in a courtyard-like spot like this?

145
00:06:58,180 --> 00:06:58,622
Yes,

146
00:06:58,672 --> 00:07:02,940
originally this whole area
was land owned by the landowner,

147
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:07,000
but the parcels were sold off one by one,
and it seems only the middle one was left.

148
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:07,600
Yes.

149
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:11,680
So Uncle Minokichi made a
living by selling off his land?

150
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,520
Well, a tiny plot like
that won't fetch much.

151
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:19,740
But those ten tsubo are the key point.

152
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:23,840
This is the project our top construction group,
Ichiryu Construction, is betting the company's future on.

153
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,520
This is the completed
design of Big Hills Mansion.

154
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:29,360
This part is sunken in.

155
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,080
Yes.

156
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:33,120
If we can't get Mr. Ryotsu's land,

157
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:36,220
we'll have to build it dented in like this.

158
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:37,080
I see, I see.

159
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:37,560
I understand.

160
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:42,840
In that case, they might pay a surprisingly
high price even for just the ten tsubo.

161
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:46,180
If a rival company were to buy this part,

162
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:48,280
it would be a repeat of the bubble era.

163
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:51,100
The president also wants
to settle this in one go.

164
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,020
Right? Right?

165
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:56,680
Maybe we could sell it for around 50 million,
couldn't we?

166
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,280
The amount our company is offering

167
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,400
How much?

168
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,540
We've staked the company's
future on the Big Hills project.

169
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:07,460
The amount the president has decided on

170
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,360
How much is it?

171
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:12,340
100 million yen for 3.3 square meters.

172
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:14,340
That comes to 1 billion yen in total.

173
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:16,380
What, 1 billion yen?

174
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,060
1 billion yen.

175
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:23,620
One billion yen

176
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:25,040
Definitely,

177
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:25,520
we'll sell it

178
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:27,440
I made my decision in 0.7 seconds.

179
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:31,060
Sorry for being so late.

180
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:32,500
Pop

181
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:34,420
We've been waiting for you.

182
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:36,880
Pop, rejoice!

183
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,000
That land sold for one billion yen!

184
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,700
What? Really?

185
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,080
No, one billion yen.

186
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:46,240
You just focus on the real estate,

187
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,680
and don't butt into family conversations.

188
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:51,480
Or I'll change my mind in 0.4 seconds.

189
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,060
Yes.

190
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:53,960
A hundred million yen or so, that's amazing.

191
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,920
It's not a dream, is it, Akankichi?

192
00:08:55,920 --> 00:09:00,500
Before Dad got here, I negotiated and pushed the price up.
Good thing

193
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:03,820
This is the contract.

194
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:06,660
Then please stamp here and here.

195
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:07,520
Yes.

196
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:11,920
Wait a moment, Dad.
I'll check the documents first.

197
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,680
Right, it's a deal.

198
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:18,140
Then, Dad, your seal here.

199
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:19,060
Here it is.

200
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,320
And here too.

201
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:23,720
Alright, that seals the deal.

202
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:25,980
Honestly.

203
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,280
So make the 100 million yen out as a cheque

204
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:30,080
and bring it to me.

205
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:32,680
Then I'll hand it over to Dad.

206
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:35,220
Make sure you don't get it wrong.

207
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:35,840
Yes.

208
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,500
I understand.

209
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:40,200
Right then, let's go, Dad.

210
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:40,900
Mm-hmm.

211
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,880
Good, good.

212
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,760
Well, if you make an enemy of me,

213
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:47,400
I'm a terrifying man, you know.

214
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:49,480
Yes, thank you very much.

215
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:52,020
Dad, that's great.

216
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,260
He really is a terrifying man.

217
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,440
Hogging 900 million yen
all to yourself like that!

218
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:10,320
What's up, Ryo-san?
Why are you grinning like that?

219
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,540
Yeah, I was grinning, wasn't I?

220
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:14,920
Did something good happen?

221
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:17,140
Well, a little.

222
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:19,800
I went and made 900 million yen.

223
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:22,360
So I'm keeping it secret from these guys.

224
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,120
Now, what to do with this money?

225
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,280
In this era of ultra-low interest rates,

226
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:29,980
putting it in savings
just to make the bank happy

227
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:30,620
would be a waste, right?

228
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:33,100
I want to do something big and flashy.

229
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:33,680
For example,

230
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,700
This one, and this one, and this one.

231
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:39,980
This one and this one.

232
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,160
I'm buying every model kit in this shop!

233
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,160
Yay!

234
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:45,640
No, that's not it.

235
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:46,980
Too small.

236
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,780
That's not a big bang at all.

237
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:51,840
Alright, I'll spend it bigger, with a bang!

238
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:58,340
Today, all machines wide open,
all for Ryotsu alone!

239
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:00,940
Jan-jan bari-bari!
Paying out until the last ball!

240
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:05,740
Shooting and shooting until
every pachinko machine is empty.

241
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:07,500
I'm going to blast away!

242
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:09,380
Cheap!

243
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,780
This is no way to spend 900 million yen.

244
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:16,340
Something that would satisfy
the playboy old man Minokichi,

245
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,020
isn't there some dreamy way to spend money?

246
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:24,900
I'm on a roll tonight!

247
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,980
Alright, I'm betting all my cash!

248
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:29,380
All of it on red 99!

249
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,280
Thank you!

250
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:33,720
Well, how about it?

251
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,780
Red 99.

252
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,580
Yes!

253
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,020
No, wait, black 1.

254
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,500
No good.

255
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:45,520
That's a total waste of money.

256
00:11:45,520 --> 00:11:47,220
Good thing it was just my imagination.

257
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:49,700
I'm pulling stars!

258
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,020
I'm back.

259
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,940
Good work.

260
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:54,360
Nothing unusual to report.

261
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,880
Let's think of a more
sensible way to spend it.

262
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:05,160
The famous English horse
Diane is going up for auction.

263
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:06,900
An English horse

264
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:08,800
As expected from the home of thoroughbreds.

265
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,000
Look at that smug face.

266
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,100
Diane? That horse?

267
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,600
You know it?

268
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:16,940
I had a friend in England who
was an incredible horse lover.

269
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:19,940
He said he wanted Diane at the next auction.

270
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:23,280
So my eye wasn't wrong after all.

271
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:27,860
Still, it's nice being rich
enough to just buy a horse.

272
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:30,000
I'm rich too, you know.

273
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:32,200
That's it, a horse!
I'll become a horse owner.

274
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:34,920
A thoroughbred will earn us loads of money!

275
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:39,560
That Diane is a descendant of Richard,
the famous horse who won the Derby.

276
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,160
It'll probably go for two million pounds.

277
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:45,840
How much is two million pounds in yen?

278
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:50,360
If the rival bids 400 million, I can win.

279
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:09,200
Nobody would ever guess that 100
million yen is hidden in this belly band.

280
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:12,200
Oku, oku, oku, 100 million!

281
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:15,700
Oh my, did something good happen?

282
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:18,660
Nothing at all. Something good
like that never happens to me.

283
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,920
Honestly, what a strange person.

284
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:26,740
Pop.

285
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:31,320
Never mind me. Use this 100
million yen however you like, Pop.

286
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,940
Just hand the whole thing over to me.

287
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:36,840
Kankichi has become a dutiful son after all.

288
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,580
Thanks to the blessings of our ancestors,

289
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:42,120
I'll gratefully spend the 100 million yen.

290
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,920
What do you mean, 100 million?

291
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:50,600
You've been acting strange since yesterday,
grinning and muttering to yourself.

292
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:53,080
Nothing, I told you.

293
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,580
Fine, if you don't want to say, I won't ask.

294
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:00,840
That's right,
I've put Yone through so much hardship.

295
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:02,740
Alright then.

296
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,540
Hey, Mom.

297
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:06,120
What is it?

298
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,940
Is there anything you want?

299
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:11,840
A ring, a handbag, anything at all.
Just say it.

300
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,080
Something I want

301
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:14,480
Yeah, something I want.

302
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:17,420
I know. I want a hardworking husband.

303
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:20,660
Really? If only you'd find a good man,
that would be something.

304
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,340
Are you going out?

305
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:27,140
Yeah. I'm no hardworking type anyway,
so I'm going to go live it up for a bit.

306
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,680
I see.

307
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,600
Now that it's come to this,
I'll blow it all in one go.

308
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:38,240
If I'm going to be a wastrel anyway,
it's Mizuguchi Daiichi-san's money.

309
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:53,660
Even though a windfall
fell right into my lap,

310
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:55,260
I don't even have the guts to spend it.

311
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:59,520
At this rate, I can't face Uncle
Minokichi or Kankitsu either.

312
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:03,860
Wow, that was a really cheap purchase.

313
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:04,840
Click!

314
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,300
Let me make the TV a little bigger.

315
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:08,520
Yes.

316
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:11,000
Today, at a British auction,

317
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,440
the star lot, Diane,
fetched a record-breaking price.

318
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:18,540
The bidding for Diane
started at 20 million yen,

319
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:23,820
but a Japanese bidder immediately bid 900 million,
so no one could compete,

320
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:26,680
and the horse was smoothly
sold to that bidder.

321
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,540
Yay!

322
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:34,000
But due to such an overly forceful approach,

323
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:38,080
it's reported that he's buying a purebred
British breed with a long tradition.

324
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:43,780
Once it's back in Japan, Diane will
quickly earn back the 900 million yen.

325
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,220
Damn them

326
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:50,620
Here he comes!

327
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:51,900
Ryo-san, a few words!

328
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:54,620
How do you feel now that you've
got the world's top racehorse?

329
00:15:56,340 --> 00:16:00,820
Even though I'm just a local civil servant,
I've worked dozens of times harder than anyone else.

330
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:05,860
To make my long-held dream of becoming a racehorse owner
come true with the 900 million yen I saved diligently,

331
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:07,680
I went over to England.

332
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:10,800
There's not a shred of
anything shady about it.

333
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:14,080
Are you really sure there's
nothing shady about it?

334
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,280
You! 900 million, five years later...
ba-ba-ba!

335
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:21,120
Don't say that,
people will get the wrong idea, everyone.

336
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:24,140
What wrong idea? Go on, explain yourself.

337
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:27,780
Listen, Dad,
the land really did sell for 1 billion yen.

338
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:31,520
But, you know, to a father who
can't even handle his 100 million yen,

339
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,600
what good is handing over 1 billion yen?

340
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,600
If you're just stashing it in your belly band,
it's all the same, isn't it?

341
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:40,060
Standing in front of the Buddhist altar,
unable to decide how to spend it,

342
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:43,700
I thought I'd buy Mom
a handbag or something.

343
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:48,580
Sure, I stormed out, but I didn't
have the guts to meet you in Ginza.

344
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:52,900
In the end, the best you'd manage is a
cold sake at your usual corner bar, right?

345
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:56,860
So you were watching?
That's why, for a father like that, I...

346
00:16:56,860 --> 00:17:01,040
took all your money and put it to
work in a dreamy asset investment.

347
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:07,380
Diane's going to win race after race for Dad.
After all, she's a true-blue thoroughbred.

348
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:10,840
Yeah, she'll earn a total of
10 billion yen in winnings.

349
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:12,520
That's the plan. We'll win.

350
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:14,580
It's not just prize money we'll bring in.

351
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:19,400
Commercial fees, movie appearance fees,
CDs, DVDs, DJ gigs...

352
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,960
W-what, that much?

353
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,880
Finally, a millionaire!

354
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:23,800
Well done!

355
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:26,200
Even Grandpa Ninokichi must be
cheering from beyond the grave.

356
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:29,260
He'd surely be moved
by your father's spirit.

357
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:31,160
Uncle Ninokichi.

358
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,980
Well done, Genki!

359
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:35,280
Keeping a racehorse, now that's admirable!

360
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:37,120
Now that's a family worth being proud of.

361
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:38,500
Uncle Ninokichi.

362
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:39,920
Thank you.

363
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,120
Just like my son!

364
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:42,220
Well done, Kankichi!

365
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:45,340
She has a fine build, doesn't she.

366
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:48,240
Well, she's as spoiled and
extravagant as they come,

367
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:51,580
so from now on she'll need a
corresponding amount for upkeep.

368
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:54,140
Dad, mind if I borrow 100 million yen?

369
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:56,780
Of course. Don't hesitate, just use it.

370
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,260
Thanks. Let's make it big together, Dad!

371
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:01,140
You bet.

372
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,760
Who would have thought Ryo-chan
would become a horse owner?

373
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:07,720
Charles, who lost the auction,
was really disappointed, you know.

374
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,880
I wonder if that horse will take to Ryo-san.

375
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:14,720
Hey, what?
You said you hate anything but a hotel?

376
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:21,880
A luxurious four-star hotel with
a view of Tokyo's night skyline.

377
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:24,900
A deluxe suite, 3 million yen per night.

378
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:30,440
It only eats English feed too. Breeding really makes a difference,
Kankichi.

379
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,780
Don't be ridiculous!

380
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:35,500
Kankichi, bring Rambo close to Mom's hand.

381
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:38,900
You still haven't repented, have you?

382
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:45,140
Damn you! I'll turn you into horse sashimi
and cherry blossom hotpot and eat you!

383
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:46,900
I told you to stop!

384
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:49,860
This horse is going to
earn me tens of billions!

385
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,800
Just put up with a few harsh words,
will you!

386
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:59,680
At this rate, he'll blow through
the remaining 100 million in no time.

387
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:02,620
We need to get Diane into
a race as soon as possible.

388
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:03,980
We've got her boxed in!

389
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,700
Run the course at full speed!

390
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:12,000
Okay, it's a test, Diane!

391
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,440
If she doesn't perform,
she's going to end up as horse sashimi.

392
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:17,120
You think I'm joking?

393
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:18,680
I'm serious.

394
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:23,920
Running while standing up.

395
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,900
Are you taking the piss, Noman?

396
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,660
But she's posting good times.

397
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:30,460
Her pace hasn't dropped at all.

398
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:30,980
What?

399
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:33,940
She's back!

400
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:35,520
What a feed!

401
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:37,580
It's a stunning new record!

402
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:37,980
What?

403
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:39,120
We did it!

404
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:41,940
But...

405
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,640
Diane, well done! Here's your feast!

406
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:51,220
Where in the world is there a racehorse
that runs on its hind legs alone?

407
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:53,140
Kankichi!

408
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:57,160
Yeah, that bastard!

409
00:19:57,160 --> 00:20:00,180
Now I see why England's racing
world got rid of that thing.

410
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,900
Boss, I could never handle that horse.

411
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:06,360
Hey, the race is coming up soon!

412
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:08,400
Please find someone else.

413
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:12,860
Since it's come to this,
you're riding it, Kankichi.

414
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:17,640
You spent 900 million yen on that worthless horse,
so take responsibility.

415
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:19,260
Fine.

416
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:29,760
How does it feel, owner,
racing your own horse?

417
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:34,360
It's an honor to race
alongside the market, Diane.

418
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:36,620
You bastard.

419
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:39,760
And now, the start of today's main race.

420
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:41,620
The only one not in the
gate is the last entrant.

421
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,820
Kanji, you've got this. Got it, Diane?

422
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:47,160
If you lose, you're getting domestic feed,
and it's nothing but veggie scraps.

423
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,300
Kanji, stage start.

424
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:50,440
No, you're late once already.

425
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:51,440
Diane too.

426
00:20:51,440 --> 00:20:53,200
Idiot, what are you doing?

427
00:20:58,340 --> 00:20:59,640
He's at it again!

428
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,360
Senpai!

429
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,860
Go for it, Ryo-chan!

430
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:05,140
Diane got off to a slow start,
but she's amazing!

431
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,060
Amazing!

432
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:07,540
Go on!

433
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:08,600
Yes!

434
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,460
Diane, from the first corner
into the second corner.

435
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:13,280
Diane has surged up to fifth place!

436
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,000
Alright!

437
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:14,980
Yes, yes!

438
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:15,720
Bakley!

439
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:17,240
Leading the way is Sun Chai New Car.

440
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:18,900
Followed by Estijina and Kamiya Hidaigo.

441
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:20,720
Diane has moved up to fourth place.

442
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,440
Rounding the fourth corner,
into the home straight.

443
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:23,960
Diane moves from third to second.

444
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:24,740
They're pulling away!

445
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:25,140
Breaking away!

446
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:26,420
Alright!

447
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:27,020
She's in the lead!

448
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,840
Diane took the lead a moment ago.

449
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:30,620
Go! Diane, go!

450
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,060
She suddenly changed her pace.

451
00:21:35,060 --> 00:21:36,480
Rounding the grandstand,

452
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:38,700
she's going with Sebastian's
Yorzeros from the start.

453
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:47,880
1st place, FD team; 2nd place,
train character; 3rd place, 3-car team

454
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:49,260
Don't you die on us, kid.

455
00:21:49,260 --> 00:21:50,480
It's not my fault.

456
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:55,740
That guy.

457
00:21:58,140 --> 00:21:59,280
From back then.

458
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:00,360
Charles.

459
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,680
Charles, long time no see.

460
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,200
Mister Nakagawa.

461
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:08,160
So you're the friend who was after Diane?

462
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:08,620
Yes.

463
00:22:08,620 --> 00:22:11,600
Charles simply couldn't give up on Diane

464
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:13,500
and apparently followed
her all the way to Japan.

465
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,320
She's my horse!
I poured 1 billion yen into her!

466
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:20,020
She's going to earn me tens
of billions from now on!

467
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:24,620
Kankichi, you'll lose money if you buy a horse you can't ride!
Sell her!

468
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,210
Yes, yes.

469
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:29,560
Charles apparently
really wants to buy Diane.

470
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:33,440
One billion!
If you offer one billion, I'll sell!

471
00:22:35,380 --> 00:22:37,120
Don't laugh! I'm serious!

472
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:39,863
Kankichi,

473
00:22:39,913 --> 00:22:43,880
we'd better get rid of her now,
before they change their minds.

474
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:46,040
How about one billion yen?

475
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:48,760
No!

476
00:22:49,180 --> 00:22:50,480
Then it's 90 million!

477
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:52,760
I won't give up a single penny more!

478
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:53,460
No!

479
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,080
85 million!

480
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:55,840
No!

481
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,560
Then it's 80 million!

482
00:22:57,780 --> 00:22:58,700
No, no!

483
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:01,380
Damn it, you're taking advantage of me!

484
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,360
She's a thoroughbred! A prize horse!

485
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:04,940
Why is it only 10,000 yen?!

486
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:07,680
This happens because you're such a slacker!

487
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:10,320
Dad, you've done nothing but complain,
so shut up!

488
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,040
It's because you went and bought a horse!

489
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:19,680
Look what you've done! I wondered
what you two were whispering about.

490
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:23,540
Mom, you know,
about Uncle Minokichi's land...

491
00:23:24,380 --> 00:23:32,480
Uncle Minokichi must be turning in his grave.
Go burn some incense with this money, you idiot father and son.

492
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,820
...is in there

493
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:34,040
Hehe.

494
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,620
Well, from a gourd comes a top

495
00:23:43,670 --> 00:23:45,780
So Tarabota's billion yen is gone

496
00:23:45,780 --> 00:23:46,691
So to speak,

497
00:23:46,741 --> 00:23:49,900
Kankichi and me, we're just a
bunch of good-for-nothing wastrels

498
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:51,689
Yeah, well,

499
00:23:51,739 --> 00:23:55,480
at least we've got the
incense money left Dad.

500
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:57,120
Yeah, that's right.

501
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:58,340
You idiots!

502
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:34,260
That strange feeling I had back then

503
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:39,480
So, the tiles of the arcade street

504
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones

505
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:53,540
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

506
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:57,560
Not the politicians with
their self-important faces

507
00:24:57,560 --> 00:25:00,880
nor the aunties who are a thorn in your side

508
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:03,860
Try turning the corner

509
00:25:04,460 --> 00:25:06,580
at that corner

510
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:11,660
You can meet everyone, everyone

511
00:25:12,180 --> 00:25:16,280
That's Kameari over there

512
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:19,580
Surely Kameari,

513
00:25:21,100 --> 00:25:24,840
come on over, everyone, to our town.

514
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:26,380
Thank you.

515
00:25:30,840 --> 00:25:34,220
Look, this is the
one-person helicopter I made!

516
00:25:34,220 --> 00:25:36,300
It's called the Shoulder Copter.

517
00:25:36,300 --> 00:25:40,280
With this, even traffic jams will ease up,
and it's sure to be a huge hit.

518
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:42,640
